# Requirements Matrix Sync Rule

When user-visible functionality changes, update `docs/REQUIREMENTS.md` in the same change.

## When updates are required

- UI flow changes in `frontend/src/App.tsx` or related frontend modules.
- API behavior changes in `backend/src/routes/` and `backend/src/services/`.
- Data model or seeded behavior changes in `backend/prisma/schema.prisma` or `backend/prisma/seed.ts`.
- Fault catalog/rules updates that affect tester behavior (`backend/src/faults/`, `docs/FAULTS.md`).
- Developer workflow changes that alter technical capabilities (scripts, test layers, CI/CD).

## How to update `docs/REQUIREMENTS.md`

- Keep structure as Epics (`EP-XX`) and User Stories (`US-XX-YY`).
- Keep acceptance criteria as concise bullet points with stable IDs:
  - `AC-US-XX-YY-N`
- Keep the scope as implemented behavior (as-is), not speculative backlog.
- Update the affected story/criteria text rather than rewriting unrelated sections.
- Maintain plain-text `Source:` tags (no markdown hyperlinks).
- Ensure each `Source:` path exists in the repository.

## Metadata upkeep

- Update the `Last synced` line at the top of `docs/REQUIREMENTS.md` with current date and commit hash.
- Preserve persona tagging and glossary consistency when adding new stories.

## Hygiene

- Do not merge user-visible behavior changes with stale requirements.
- Treat requirements drift as a documentation bug.
